Differents output formats that nmap provides.
OUTPUT formats:

-oN //Normal format, save the results with the format that we've typically seen on the terminal.

-oX //XML format, we can save the nmap results to a XML formats and import them to the Metasploit Framework database,
and have all relevant information about the target. That make esier to have a centralise view of the target.

To import the -oX, XML format file into our Metasploit Framework Database, we need to perform PostgreSQL database, because Metasploit database requires to
connect to the PostgreSQL.

We need to input those commands on the terminal
service postgresql start
msfconsole
workspace -a pentest_1 // use workspace -h to show the commands
workspace
db_status //To check the database status, in this case, it should output "Connected to msf. Connection type: postgresql."
db_import <file.xml> //Specify the PATH and the xml format file that we need to import
hosts //To show target information that we import with the xml format file on the previous step.
services // To show the open ports that is running on the target system that we import with the xml format file on the previous step.

Run the nmap command within metasploit
db_nmap -Pn -sS -sV -O -p445 <TARGET>
//When we utilize the db_nmap command within the metasploit framework, the scan results will be automatically saved in the metasploit framework
within the current work space that we operating in.

-oS //Script kiddie format

-oG //Grepable format, using grep.

-oA <basename> //Allows output our scan results in the 3 major formats at once (-oN, -oX, -oG)

-v //Increase amount of information display to our terminal when we performing the scan.

